**Pattern:** Floyd's fast & slow pointers.

- Move slow 1, fast 2; meeting ⇒ cycle
- To find start: reset one pointer to head, move both by 1; they meet at the entry
- O(n) time, O(1) space

**Java**

```java
ListNode detectCycle(ListNode head) {
    ListNode slow = head, fast = head;
    while (fast != null && fast.next != null) {
        slow = slow.next;
        fast = fast.next.next;
        if (slow == fast) { // meet inside the cycle
            ListNode p = head;
            while (p != slow) { p = p.next; slow = slow.next; }
            return p; // cycle start
        }
    }
    return null;
}
```

