        if slow is fast:  # meet inside the cycle
            p = head
            while p is not slow:
                p, slow = p.next, slow.next
            return p  # cycle start
    return None
```

**Pattern:** middle + reverse + merge.

1. Find middle with fast/slow
2. Reverse the second half (cut first!)
3. Alternate-merge the two halves
- O(n), O(1) space

**Java**

```java
void reorderList(ListNode head) {
    ListNode slow = head, fast = head;
    while (fast != null && fast.next != null) { slow = slow.next; fast = fast.next.next; }
    ListNode prev = null, cur = slow.next; // reverse second half
    slow.next = null;
    while (cur != null) { ListNode nx = cur.next; cur.next = prev; prev = cur; cur = nx; }
    for (ListNode a = head, b = prev; b != null; ) { // weave
        ListNode an = a.next, bn = b.next;
        a.next = b; b.next = an;
        a = an; b = bn;
    }
}
```

