    while fast and fast.next:
        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next
    prev, cur = None, slow.next  # reverse second half
    slow.next = None
    while cur:
        cur.next, prev, cur = prev, cur, cur.next
    a, b = head, prev
    while b:  # weave
        an, bn = a.next, b.next
        a.next, b.next = b, an
        a, b = an, bn
```

- Height, diameter, path sums, subtree properties → **DFS** returning a value
- Level by level, right-side view, min depth → **BFS** with a queue
- BST: sorted order → **inorder** traversal; search by comparing values
- LCA, serialize/deserialize, build from traversals

**Java**

```java
// DFS: path / subtree answers. BFS: level-by-level / shortest depth.
int minDepth(TreeNode root) { // BFS stops at the first leaf
    if (root == null) return 0;
    Deque<TreeNode> q = new ArrayDeque<>(List.of(root));
    for (int depth = 1; ; depth++) {
        for (int n = q.size(); n > 0; n--) {
            TreeNode t = q.poll();
            if (t.left == null && t.right == null) return depth;
            if (t.left != null) q.offer(t.left);
            if (t.right != null) q.offer(t.right);
        }
    }
}
```

