**Pattern:** backtracking with reuse.

- Sort candidates; `dfs(start, remaining)`
- For `i ≥ start`: if `c[i] > remaining` break; choose, `dfs(i, remaining - c[i])`, un-choose
- `remaining == 0` → record copy

**Java**

```java
List<List<Integer>> combinationSum(int[] c, int target) {
    List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
    go(c, 0, target, new ArrayList<>(), res);
    return res;
}

void go(int[] c, int i, int left, List<Integer> path, List<List<Integer>> res) {
    if (left == 0) { res.add(new ArrayList<>(path)); return; }
    if (left < 0 || i == c.length) return;
    path.add(c[i]);
    go(c, i, left - c[i], path, res);  // reuse c[i]
    path.remove(path.size() - 1);
    go(c, i + 1, left, path, res);     // move past c[i]
}
```

