**Pattern:** DP, or patience sorting.

- O(n²): `dp[i] = 1 + max(dp[j])` for j < i with `a[j] < a[i]`
- O(n log n): keep `tails`; binary-search the first tail ≥ x and replace it (or append)
- Answer = tails size

**Java**

```java
int lengthOfLIS(int[] nums) { // O(n log n) patience sorting
    int[] tails = new int[nums.length];
    int len = 0;
    for (int x : nums) {
        int i = Arrays.binarySearch(tails, 0, len, x);
        if (i < 0) i = -(i + 1); // insertion point
        tails[i] = x;
        if (i == len) len++;
    }
    return len;
}
```

