**Pattern:** shrinking boundaries.

- `top, bottom, left, right`
- Right along top (top++), down right col (right--)
- If `top <= bottom`: left along bottom (bottom--)
- If `left <= right`: up left col (left++)
- Repeat while in bounds; O(m·n)

**Java**

```java
List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] m) {
    List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
    int top = 0, bot = m.length - 1, left = 0, right = m[0].length - 1;
    while (top <= bot && left <= right) {
        for (int j = left; j <= right; j++) res.add(m[top][j]);
        top++;
        for (int i = top; i <= bot; i++) res.add(m[i][right]);
        right--;
        if (top <= bot) { for (int j = right; j >= left; j--) res.add(m[bot][j]); bot--; }
        if (left <= right) { for (int i = bot; i >= top; i--) res.add(m[i][left]); left++; }
    }
    return res;
}
```

**Python**

```python
def spiral_order(m):
    res = []
    while m:
        res += m.pop(0)               # take top row
        m = [list(r) for r in zip(*m)][::-1]  # rotate rest counter-clockwise
    return res
```

- Every element appears twice except one → **XOR**
- Count set bits, power of two, reverse bits
- "Without using + or −" → XOR + carry
- O(1) extra space with pairing/cancellation
- Subsets as masks when n ≤ ~20

**Java**

```java
// Signal: XOR cancels pairs, masks for subsets, O(1) space tricks.
List<List<Integer>> subsetsByMask(int[] nums) {
    List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << nums.length); mask++) {
        List<Integer> s = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++)
            if ((mask >> i & 1) == 1) s.add(nums[i]);
        res.add(s);
    }
    return res;
}
```

**Python**

```python
# Signal: XOR cancels pairs, masks for subsets, O(1) space tricks.
def subsets_by_mask(nums):
    n = len(nums)
    return [[nums[i] for i in range(n) if mask >> i & 1]
            for mask in range(1 << n)]
```

**Java**

```java
int singleNumber(int[] nums) {
    int x = 0;
    for (int v : nums) x ^= v; // pairs cancel
    return x;
}

int popcount(int n) {
    int c = 0;
    while (n != 0) { n &= n - 1; c++; } // clear lowest set bit
    return c;
}

boolean isPowerOfTwo(int n) { return n > 0 && (n & (n - 1)) == 0; }

int[] countBits(int n) {
    int[] dp = new int[n + 1];
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i] = dp[i >> 1] + (i & 1);
    return dp;
}
```

